  "date_id": "2025-11-09",
  "fcc_description": "<p>Given a matrix (an array of arrays) of single letters and a word to find, return the start and end indices of the word in the matrix.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>The given matrix will be filled with all lowercase letters (<code>a-z</code>).</li>\n<li>The word to find will always be in the matrix exactly once.</li>\n<li>The word to find will always be in a straight line in one of these directions:\n<ul>\n<li>left to right</li>\n<li>right to left</li>\n<li>top to bottom</li>\n<li>bottom to top</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>For example, given the matrix:</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-md\">[\n  [\"a\", \"c\", \"t\"],\n  [\"t\", \"a\", \"t\"],\n  [\"c\", \"t\", \"c\"]\n]\n</code></pre>\n<p>And the word <code>\"cat\"</code>, return:</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-md\">[[0, 1], [2, 1]]\n</code></pre>\n<p>Where <code>[0, 1]</code> are the indices for the <code>\"c\"</code> (start of the word), and <code>[2, 1]</code> are the indices for the <code>\"t\"</code> (end of the word).</p>",
  "fcc_js_tests": "[{\"text\": \"<p><code>findWord([[\\\"a\\\", \\\"c\\\", \\\"t\\\"], [\\\"t\\\", \\\"a\\\", \\\"t\\\"], [\\\"c\\\", \\\"t\\\", \\\"c\\\"]], \\\"cat\\\")</code> should return <code>[[0, 1], [2, 1]]</code>.</p>\", \"testString\": \"assert.deepEqual(findWord([[\\\"a\\\", \\\"c\\\", \\\"t\\\"], [\\\"t\\\", \\\"a\\\", \\\"t\\\"], [\\\"c\\\", \\\"t\\\", \\\"c\\\"]], \\\"cat\\\"), [[0, 1], [2, 1]]);\"}, {\"text\": \"<p><code>findWord([[\\\"d\\\", \\\"o\\\", \\\"g\\\"], [\\\"o\\\", \\\"g\\\", \\\"d\\\"], [\\\"d\\\", \\\"g\\\", \\\"o\\\"]], \\\"dog\\\")</code> should return <code>[[0, 0], [0, 2]]</code>.</p>\", \"testString\": \"assert.deepEqual(findWord([[\\\"d\\\", \\\"o\\\", \\\"g\\\"], [\\\"o\\\", \\\"g\\\", \\\"d\\\"], [\\\"d\\\", \\\"g\\\", \\\"o\\\"]], \\\"dog\\\"), [[0, 0], [0, 2]]);\"}, {\"text\": \"<p><code>findWord([[\\\"h\\\", \\\"i\\\", \\\"s\\\", \\\"h\\\"], [\\\"i\\\", \\\"s\\\", \\\"f\\\", \\\"s\\\"], [\\\"f\\\", \\\"s\\\", \\\"i\\\", \\\"i\\\"], [\\\"s\\\", \\\"h\\\", \\\"i\\\", \\\"f\\\"]], \\\"fish\\\")</code> should return <code>[[3, 3], [0, 3]]</code>.</p>\", \"testString\": \"assert.deepEqual(findWord([[\\\"h\\\", \\\"i\\\", \\\"s\\\", \\\"h\\\"], [\\\"i\\\", \\\"s\\\", \\\"f\\\", \\\"s\\\"], [\\\"f\\\", \\\"s\\\", \\\"i\\\", \\\"i\\\"], [\\\"s\\\", \\\"h\\\", \\\"i\\\", \\\"f\\\"]], \\\"fish\\\"), [[3, 3], [0, 3]]);\"}, {\"text\": \"<p><code>findWord([[\\\"f\\\", \\\"x\\\", \\\"o\\\", \\\"x\\\"], [\\\"o\\\", \\\"x\\\", \\\"o\\\", \\\"f\\\"], [\\\"f\\\", \\\"o\\\", \\\"f\\\", \\\"x\\\"], [\\\"f\\\", \\\"x\\\", \\\"x\\\", \\\"o\\\"]], \\\"fox\\\")</code> should return <code>[[1, 3], [1, 1]]</code>.</p>\", \"testString\": \"assert.deepEqual(findWord([[\\\"f\\\", \\\"x\\\", \\\"o\\\", \\\"x\\\"], [\\\"o\\\", \\\"x\\\", \\\"o\\\", \\\"f\\\"], [\\\"f\\\", \\\"o\\\", \\\"f\\\", \\\"x\\\"], [\\\"f\\\", \\\"x\\\", \\\"x\\\", \\\"o\\\"]], \\\"fox\\\"), [[1, 3], [1, 1]]);\"}]",
  "fcc_py_tests": "[{\"text\": \"<p><code>find_word([[\\\"a\\\", \\\"c\\\", \\\"t\\\"], [\\\"t\\\", \\\"a\\\", \\\"t\\\"], [\\\"c\\\", \\\"t\\\", \\\"c\\\"]], \\\"cat\\\")</code> should return <code>[[0, 1], [2, 1]]</code>.</p>\", \"testString\": \"({test: () => { runPython(`\\nfrom unittest import TestCase\\nTestCase().assertEqual(find_word([[\\\"a\\\", \\\"c\\\", \\\"t\\\"], [\\\"t\\\", \\\"a\\\", \\\"t\\\"], [\\\"c\\\", \\\"t\\\", \\\"c\\\"]], \\\"cat\\\"), [[0, 1], [2, 1]])`)\\n}})\"}, {\"text\": \"<p><code>find_word([[\\\"d\\\", \\\"o\\\", \\\"g\\\"], [\\\"o\\\", \\\"g\\\", \\\"d\\\"], [\\\"d\\\", \\\"g\\\", \\\"o\\\"]], \\\"dog\\\")</code> should return <code>[[0, 0], [0, 2]]</code>.</p>\", \"testString\": \"({test: () => { runPython(`\\nfrom unittest import TestCase\\nTestCase().assertEqual(find_word([[\\\"d\\\", \\\"o\\\", \\\"g\\\"], [\\\"o\\\", \\\"g\\\", \\\"d\\\"], [\\\"d\\\", \\\"g\\\", \\\"o\\\"]], \\\"dog\\\"), [[0, 0], [0, 2]])`)\\n}})\"}, {\"text\": \"<p><code>find_word([[\\\"h\\\", \\\"i\\\", \\\"s\\\", \\\"h\\\"], [\\\"i\\\", \\\"s\\\", \\\"f\\\", \\\"s\\\"], [\\\"f\\\", \\\"s\\\", \\\"i\\\", \\\"i\\\"], [\\\"s\\\", \\\"h\\\", \\\"i\\\", \\\"f\\\"]], \\\"fish\\\")</code> should return <code>[[3, 3], [0, 3]]</code>.</p>\", \"testString\": \"({test: () => { runPython(`\\nfrom unittest import TestCase\\nTestCase().assertEqual(find_word([[\\\"h\\\", \\\"i\\\", \\\"s\\\", \\\"h\\\"], [\\\"i\\\", \\\"s\\\", \\\"f\\\", \\\"s\\\"], [\\\"f\\\", \\\"s\\\", \\\"i\\\", \\\"i\\\"], [\\\"s\\\", \\\"h\\\", \\\"i\\\", \\\"f\\\"]], \\\"fish\\\"), [[3, 3], [0, 3]])`)\\n}})\"}, {\"text\": \"<p><code>find_word([[\\\"f\\\", \\\"x\\\", \\\"o\\\", \\\"x\\\"], [\\\"o\\\", \\\"x\\\", \\\"o\\\", \\\"f\\\"], [\\\"f\\\", \\\"o\\\", \\\"f\\\", \\\"x\\\"], [\\\"f\\\", \\\"x\\\", \\\"x\\\", \\\"o\\\"]], \\\"fox\\\")</code> should return <code>[[1, 3], [1, 1]]</code>.</p>\", \"testString\": \"({test: () => { runPython(`\\nfrom unittest import TestCase\\nTestCase().assertEqual(find_word([[\\\"f\\\", \\\"x\\\", \\\"o\\\", \\\"x\\\"], [\\\"o\\\", \\\"x\\\", \\\"o\\\", \\\"f\\\"], [\\\"f\\\", \\\"o\\\", \\\"f\\\", \\\"x\\\"], [\\\"f\\\", \\\"x\\\", \\\"x\\\", \\\"o\\\"]], \\\"fox\\\"), [[1, 3], [1, 1]])`)\\n}})\"}]",
